  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1033 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nHOT AND DRY CONDITIONS CONTINUE:\n\nTemperatures cool slightly on Wednesday, thanks to a weak wave \nrotating around the high centered over the Southwest. Temperatures \nwill only be a few degrees cooler, with the Desert Valleys seeing \nupper-90s to low-100s and the higher elevations seeing 70s to low \n80s. This is enough to finally provide one Heat Advisory free day. \nHowever, as the high pressure continues to build into the southern \nGreat Basin into the weekend, temperatures climb once more. Near-\nrecord afternoon highs return for Friday into the weekend. \nAdditionally, the western placement of the high keeps eastern Utah \nand western Colorado disconnected from any monsoonal moisture, \nkeeping things dry. There is a non-zero chance for an isolated \nshower or thunderstorm over the southern and central Divide through \nthe end of the week, but extremely dry surface levels keep wetting \nrain chances near-zero, with the main concerns with any storms being \nlightning and gusty winds. \n\nLooking into early next week, models continue to hint at a stronger \ntrough moving onto the West Coast, displacing the center of the high \nback to the east. This opens to door for some monsoonal moisture to \nreturn to the Four Corners region into mid-next week. So stay tuned, \nwe may finally see some relief from the heat.\n\nFIRE WEATHER:\n\nHigh pressure sticking around will keep hot and dry weather in the \nforecast through the end of the week and into the weekend. On \nWednesday, a jet clips the northeast corner of the CWA, bumping up \nwinds and bringing 25-35 mph gusts. Widespread Critical Fire Weather \nconditions are expected for zones along the Central Divide, and Red \nFlag Warnings are in effect from 1PM to 8PM. Elsewhere, winds will \nbe borderline, therefore only localized Critical Fire Weather \nConditions are expected. The jet moves east by Thursday, with the \noverall pressure gradient aloft relaxing. Deep mixing will help to \nbring down some stronger gusts to around 25 mph, especially along \nthe Central Divide and around the Four Corners. However, with these \nmarginal wind gusts, only localized Critical Fire Weather Conditions \nare anticipated at this time. Friday looks to follow a similar \npattern.",
